{"id": "language-p04564", "blocks": [{"id": "language-p04564", "text": "Gate 4D — Coverage and Ambiguity Measurement 1.0", "style": "HEADING_1", "sourceParagraph": 4564}, {"id": "language-p04565", "text": "Status: COMPLETE — CANONICAL MEASUREMENT RELEASE", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4565}, {"id": "language-p04566", "text": "Measured inventory: 436 senses / 419 lemmas", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4566}, {"id": "language-p04567", "text": "Direct atom mappings: 358", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4567}, {"id": "language-p04568", "text": "Direct compound mappings: 35", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4568}, {"id": "language-p04569", "text": "Future grammar routes: 8", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4569}, {"id": "language-p04570", "text": "Future semantic-IR routes: 24", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4570}, {"id": "language-p04571", "text": "Explicit unsupported gaps: 11", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4571}, {"id": "language-p04572", "text": "Coverage results", "style": "HEADING_2", "sourceParagraph": 4572}, {"id": "language-p04573", "text": "• Direct lexical coverage: 90.14% of indexed senses.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4573}, {"id": "language-p04574", "text": "• Structurally routed coverage, including future grammar and IR: 97.48%.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4574}, {"id": "language-p04575", "text": "• Explicit gap share: 2.52%.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4575}, {"id": "language-p04576", "text": "• Exact controlled-label coverage: 100% for every atom and approved compound.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4576}, {"id": "language-p04577", "text": "• Reviewed high-frequency layer: 48.81% directly lexical, 86.90% eventually expressible after grammar/IR, and 13.10% explicit gaps.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4577}, {"id": "language-p04578", "text": "Ambiguity results", "style": "HEADING_2", "sourceParagraph": 4578}, {"id": "language-p04579", "text": "Forty-one of 419 normalized lemmas (9.79%) require disambiguation or nonlexical routing. Five lemmas have more than one direct canonical target. A future translator must never select the first candidate: it must use controlled sense IDs, contextual constraints, ranked candidates, or clarification.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4579}, {"id": "language-p04580", "text": "Release boundary and next work", "style": "HEADING_2", "sourceParagraph": 4580}, {"id": "language-p04581", "text": "Gates 4C and 4D do not authorize an English parser or translator. The next authorized gate is Gate 4E, the etymology table. Semantic IR, executable grammar, deterministic renderer, inverse decoder, controlled-English compiler, and general-English translator remain unstarted.", "style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "sourceParagraph": 4581}], "outline": [{"id": "language-p04564", "title": "Gate 4D — Coverage and Ambiguity Measurement 1.0", "level": 1}, {"id": "language-p04572", "title": "Coverage results", "level": 2}, {"id": "language-p04578", "title": "Ambiguity results", "level": 2}, {"id": "language-p04580", "title": "Release boundary and next work", "level": 2}]}